{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ChiralityResidueMassTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ChiralityResidueMassTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chirality_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chirality_residue","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-residue-mass-term.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**Chirality residue is the predicate split with `P = is_chirality`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_tower_split_by_predicate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_tower_split_by_predicate","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-residue-mass-term.lean#L35-L56","doc":"**Mass tower split.**  For any predicate `P` on partitions, the\nmass tower decomposes as the sum over `P λ` plus the sum over\n`¬ P λ`.  When `P = is_chirality`, this gives the chirality /\nnon-chirality split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.is_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.is_chirality","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-residue-mass-term.lean#L31-L33","doc":"Chirality predicate: `c_λ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.signed_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.signed_content","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/chirality-residue-mass-term.lean#L24-L29","doc":"Signed Young content of a partition `λ`: `c_λ = Σ_{(i,j) ∈ λ}(j − i)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}